{"metadata": {"version": "0.3.3", "copyright": "Copyright (c) 2026 graineo project; format and method by Andrea Volpato (spektrafilm). Licensed under CC BY-SA 4.0.", "created": "2026-10-29", "license": "spektrafilm profile by Andrea Volpato, licensed under CC BY-SA 4.0. Redistribution and derivatives must credit the author, link the project (https://github.com/andreavolpato/spektrafilm),preserve this license, and remain CC BY-SA 4.0.Modifications must be noted. Full text of the license and attribution requirements: https://github.com/andreavolpato/spektrafilm/blob/main/SPEKTRAFILM_LICENSE.txt.", "citation": "If you use this profile in your work, please cite the spektrafilm project: https://github.com/andreavolpato/spektrafilm, see CITATION.cff for details.", "datasource": "Characteristic curves (Status A, daylight 1/100 s), spectral sensitivity and spectral dye density curves digitised from the Kodak data sheet E-28 (KODAK PROFESSIONAL EKTACHROME Film E200, 9/2005, page 5). Original data are property of Eastman Kodak Company. Exposure axis shifted by log10(14.5/200) so that 0 is mid-grey at ISO 200; net density = density minus minimum. The sheet gives no minimum-density spectrum for this film: base density takes the shape of the Ektachrome E100 profile (same process E-6), scaled by the ratio of the curve minima. Mid-grey neutral density = visual-neutral dye curve of the sheet scaled by 0.732 (factor found in the official E100 profile). Density scale a and adaptation window follow the graineo reversal-film family rule, standard dyes adapted to the mid-grey spectrum. Derived from spektrafilm profile format; modified by graineo.", "modifications": "New profile created from manufacturer data by the graineo project; only the profile format, wavelength grid, dye-family form and base-density shape taken from spektrafilm profiles."}, "info": {"type": "positive", "support": "film", "stage": "filming", "use": "still", "antihalation": "strong", "target_print": null, "channel_model": "color", "densitometer": "status_A", "log_sensitivity_density_over_min": 0.2, "reference_illuminant": "D55", "viewing_illuminant": "D50", "name": "Kodak Ektachrome E200", "card": {"maker": "Kodak", "iso": 200, "type": "Farbumkehrfilm (Dia, E-6)", "rms": 12, "additional": "Datenblatt E-28", "text": "Das Dia mit ISO 200 und der Anmutung eines langsameren Films: moderate Kontraste, nat\u00fcrliche Hautt\u00f6ne und feines Korn. Das Blatt nennt Push-Entwicklung bis EI 800; sie ist hier nicht abgebildet.", "source": "Kodak E-28", "process": "E-6", "period": "Einstellung am 4. Februar 2011 angek\u00fcndigt", "suitable": ["Reportage bei wenig Licht", "Sport am Tag", "Portr\u00e4t mit nat\u00fcrlichen Farben"], "less_suitable": ["sehr feine Vergr\u00f6\u00dferungen", "knallige Landschaftsfarben"], "tips": ["Diafilm: kein Papier. F\u00fcr den Dia-Look die Filmbelichtung exakt setzen (kleine Schritte).", "F\u00fcr mehr Zeichnung in den Schatten die Filmbelichtung leicht anheben."], "facts": [{"text": "Das Datenblatt stellt E200 als ersten schnellen Diafilm mit dem Aussehen eines langsameren Films vor: T-Grain-Emulsionen, m\u00e4\u00dfiger Kontrast und Push-Entwicklung bis EI 800 mit nur geringen Verschiebungen von Kontrast und Farbbalance.", "source": "Kodak E-28 (September 2005)"}, {"text": "Kodak k\u00fcndigte am 4. Februar 2011 die Einstellung von Ektachrome 200 an.", "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kodak_Ektachrome"}]}, "stock": "kodak_ektachrome_e200"}, "data": {"wavelengths": [380.0, 385.0, 390.0, 395.0, 400.0, 405.0, 410.0, 415.0, 420.0, 425.0, 430.0, 435.0, 440.0, 445.0, 450.0, 455.0, 460.0, 465.0, 470.0, 475.0, 480.0, 485.0, 490.0, 495.0, 500.0, 505.0, 510.0, 515.0, 520.0, 525.0, 530.0, 535.0, 540.0, 545.0, 550.0, 555.0, 560.0, 565.0, 570.0, 575.0, 580.0, 585.0, 590.0, 595.0, 600.0, 605.0, 610.0, 615.0, 620.0, 625.0, 630.0, 635.0, 640.0, 645.0, 650.0, 655.0, 660.0, 665.0, 670.0, 675.0, 680.0, 685.0, 690.0, 695.0, 700.0, 705.0, 710.0, 715.0, 720.0, 725